\examples{
# The industrialization and Political Democracy Example from Bollen (1989), page
# 332
model <- "
  # Latent variable definitions
     ind60 =~ x1 + x2 + x3
     dem60 =~ y1 + a*y2 + b*y3 + c*y4
     dem65 =~ y5 + a*y6 + b*y7 + c*y8

  # (Latent) regressions
    dem60 ~ ind60
    dem65 ~ ind60 + dem60

  # Residual correlations
    y1 ~~ y5
    y2 ~~ y4 + y6
    y3 ~~ y7
    y4 ~~ y8
    y6 ~~ y8
"
utils::data("PoliticalDemocracy", package = "lavaan")

fit <- asem(model, PoliticalDemocracy, test = "none")
summary(fit)
}
\seealso{
Typically, users will interact with the specific latent variable
model functions instead, including \code{\link[=acfa]{acfa()}}, \code{\link[=asem]{asem()}}, and \code{\link[=agrowth]{agrowth()}}.
